Company Introduction:

Airspace is a tech-enabled freight forwarder that’s redefining how the world’s most critical packages are delivered. Headquartered in Carlsbad, California, Airspace has employees who are based around the world. Our European headquarters is in Amsterdam, The Netherlands.

As a recognized leader in AI and machine learning, our team leverages data and patented technology to coordinate logistics across a global network of drivers and airlines. Our goal is to deliver those packages that are truly mission-critical in a way that is faster, more transparent, more secure, and more accountable than ever before. The items we deliver range from organs for transplant, to parts for critical machinery including grounded aircraft and highly sensitive components such as semiconductors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Airspace has been rated one of&nbsp; America’s best Startup Employers and listed as one of&nbsp; CNBC’s Disruptor 50 companies. Airspace has the support of leading investors such as Telstra Ventures, HarbourVest Partners, Defy Partners, DBL Partners, and Scale Ventures. To date the company has raised more than $140m.&nbsp;

The company is growing rapidly and serving more places around the world than ever before. We are looking for passionate, motivated individuals who want to make an IMPACT every day to help us execute on our mission of reshaping the world of time-critical logistics.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Own Driver Engagement in Your Region&nbsp;

The Commander Coordinator is the person who makes sure Airspace’s driver network in a region runs well day to day. Where the Regional Network Manager owns the complete supply picture for the region - strategy, agent partners, and escalation - the Commander Coordinator owns the direct, ongoing relationship with every Commander and Copilot driver in that region: keeping Tier 1 drivers engaged, Tier 2 drivers progressing, and Tier 3 drivers identified and resolved before they affect service.

This is a support role to the Regional Network Manager, not a standalone strategy seat. You are the direct line to drivers - the person they know, trust, and call - and the person your Regional NM depends on to know the true state of the driver pool in the region at any given time.&nbsp;

Like agent support, driver support is a tiered model - attention scales with where a driver sits in the network rather than spreading evenly across the whole population. Tier 1 drivers get high-touch, relationship-driven attention. Tier 2 gets consistent, standard engagement and onboarding support. Tier 3 gets focused attention aimed at surfacing issues early and, once authorized, executing deactivation cleanly. Getting that allocation right is the core judgment call in this role.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

What You’ll Do&nbsp;

Tier 1 Drivers (High performers)&nbsp;

• Provide high-touch support to Tier 1 Commander and Copilot drivers, including regular check-ins to maintain engagement, address concerns, and reinforce performance standards&nbsp;

• Serve as the primary point of contact for Tier 1 drivers in your region&nbsp;

Tier 2 Drivers (General population &amp; new drivers)&nbsp;

• Support the general driver population and new drivers through onboarding, ramp guidance, and routine engagement - helping drivers build familiarity with Airspace standards and expectations early&nbsp;

• Monitor Tier 2 performance through automated reporting, flagging drivers trending toward Tier 3 before issues escalate&nbsp;

Tier 3 Drivers (Performance and conduct - managed out)&nbsp;

• Identify and surface Tier 3 drivers - those whose behavior, reliability, or conduct warrants removal from the network - using automated reporting and case data&nbsp;

• Execute deactivation motions once authorized by the Regional Network Manager, managing the workflow through Salesforce case management&nbsp;

General&nbsp;

• Manage the driver case queue in Salesforce, triaging and routing escalations and maintaining accurate records for your region&nbsp;

